{"id":"nf5503d5c1b","headline":"Central banks turn hawkish again as oil shock stokes inflation","summary":"Interest rate hikes are becoming a global trend, the longest monetary tightening since 2023. The West Asia oil shock has pushed headline inflation higher in major economies, and the Fed and Bank of England are expected to raise rates this week.","why":"Central banks set policy interest rates that influence borrowing costs, bond yields, currencies and equity valuations worldwide. Energy-driven inflation often forces them to tighten policy.","category":"economy","event_type":"rates","importance":3,"flag":null,"market_moving":true,"location":{"place":"Washington","country":"United States of America","lat":38.9,"lon":-77.04,"region":"na"},"entities":[],"links":[],"source":{"name":"The Economic Times","url":"https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/us-stocks/news/central-banks-resume-interest-rate-hikes-amid-oil-shock-and-rising-inflation-trends/articleshow/134250003.cms"},"sources":[{"name":"The Economic Times","url":"https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/us-stocks/news/central-banks-resume-interest-rate-hikes-amid-oil-shock-and-rising-inflation-trends/articleshow/134250003.cms"}],"published_at":"2026-09-15T02:10:00Z","retrieved_at":"2026-11-12T08:33:11Z","official":false,"ai_summary":true,"content_hash":"8b389446d05e3671","impacts":[],"why_moved":null,"backfilled":true,"backfilled_at":"2026-11-12T08:33:11Z","backfill_provenance":{"version":"gdelt-backfill-v1","original_published_at":"2026-09-15T02:10:00Z","feed_url":"https://data.gdeltproject.org/gdeltv2/","discovered_via":"GDELT GKG 2.1","gdelt_seen":"2026-09-15T03:00:00Z","publisher_country_gdelt":"JA","description_from":"publisher page metadata"},"image":{"kind":"topic","file":"photos/central-bank-building-4765706.jpg","alt":"central bank building (illustration)","credit":"Makalu","license":"Pixabay Content License","license_url":"https://pixabay.com/service/license-summary/","source":"Pixabay","sour